<section id="founder" class="border-y border-line bg-paper-alt px-6 py-20 md:px-10 md:py-28">
  <div class="mx-auto grid max-w-wrap gap-12 md:grid-cols-2 md:gap-16">
    <div class="reveal">
      <p class="font-mono text-xs uppercase tracking-widest2 text-amber">As a builder</p>
      <h3 class="mt-3 font-display text-2xl font-semibold text-ink md:text-3xl">
        I take a rough idea straight to a working interface.
      </h3>
      <p class="mt-4 text-[15px] leading-relaxed text-ink-soft">
        No Figma handoff needed — I design in the browser. Frontend architecture,
        anime.js-driven interaction, Supabase schemas and API wiring, deployment.
        I've debugged stale auth roles, redirect loops, and a Vercel build that
        died over a missing environment variable, all in the same week.
      </p>
      <ul class="mt-6 space-y-2 font-mono text-[12.5px] text-ink-soft">
        <li>→ React, AstroJS, Tailwind CSS, anime.js</li>
        <li>→ Node.js, Supabase / PostgreSQL</li>
        <li>→ React Native / Expo, basic Arduino</li>
        <li>→ Linux / Debian administration</li>
      </ul>
    </div>

    <div class="reveal" style="--reveal-delay:100ms">
      <p class="font-mono text-xs uppercase tracking-widest2 text-moss">As a founder</p>
      <h3 class="mt-3 font-display text-2xl font-semibold text-ink md:text-3xl">
        UniPulse started as a gap I kept running into.
      </h3>
      <p class="mt-4 text-[15px] leading-relaxed text-ink-soft">
        University of Ilorin had no single place to get campus news and
        resources to students fast. So I designed UniPulse to fix that —
        information and resource-sharing first, with an events feed as one
        feature inside it, not the point of the app. I built it myself and
        I'm still the one debugging the queries at 1am. Separately, I work
        inside Aoni as a developer on JUT — close enough to see how a second
        company gets built from day one.
      </p>
      <ul class="mt-6 space-y-2 font-mono text-[12.5px] text-ink-soft">
        <li>→ Product scope, not just implementation</li>
        <li>→ Own the roadmap end-to-end at UniPulse</li>
        <li>→ Shipped inside Aoni as a contributor, not a founder</li>
        <li>→ Comfortable owning ambiguity when there's no spec</li>
      </ul>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>
